# The Style-Token Guard

A design system where "components read tokens, never raw hex" is only as good as
its enforcement. osionos enforces it with **`scripts/check-style-tokens.sh`** — a
small, dependency-free shell guard that runs as the **final step of the quality
gate** (`npm run test:quality`).

> [!success] The rule it protects
> Colour **values** live only in the token-definition files under
> `src/app/styles/**` (chiefly `global.css`). Every other app CSS/SCSS surface must
> reference `var(--osio-*)`. The guard fails the build if a raw literal escapes.

## What counts as a violation

The guard greps every app-authored `.css` / `.scss` file for a **bare colour
literal** — a `#hex` (3–8 chars) or an `rgb()` / `rgba()` with numeric channels:

```
✗ raw colour literal(s) in src/features/foo/foo.scss (use var(--osio-*)):
    42:  color: #3355ff;
```

What is **allowed**, because it references a token, not a literal:

```scss
background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--osio-accent) 14%, transparent); /* ✓ */
border-color: var(--osio-border-default);                            /* ✓ */
```

## What it deliberately skips

| Scanned | Excluded |
|:--------|:---------|
| all app-authored `src/**/*.{css,scss}` | `src/app/styles/**` — the canonical token files |
| feature + widget styles | `notion-database-sys` — vendored, own gate |
| — | `lib/markengine` — vendored, own gate |

The token files are excluded because they are *supposed* to hold the hex values;
the vendored trees have their own toolchains.

## Why dependency-free

> [!info] No stylelint on purpose
> osionos runs a locked-down supply chain (7-day release-age hold, frozen
> lockfiles). A guard that needs no npm plugin can't be a supply-chain liability,
> and it runs the same on any machine with `bash`.

## Running it

```sh
bash scripts/check-style-tokens.sh          # standalone
npm run test:quality                        # runs it last, after tsc + eslint
```

- [x] Passes silently with `✓ style-token check passed`.
- [x] Fails with the exact `file:line` of every raw literal.
- [x] Exit code gates the whole `test:quality` run.

This guard is what lets [eight palettes](./color-palettes.xmd) and
[two modes](./light-dark-theming.xmd) stay coherent: no component can quietly
hard-code a colour that a palette switch would then fail to recolour.
